    {
      "id": "sec_bnwb98q1td",
      "preset": "component/bff-story@1",
      "label": "When systems fail",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "content"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "light",
        "background": {
          "type": "color",
          "color": "#e9e6d2"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_80rxh5px12",
          "type": "component/bff-story",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "heading": "When systems fail, people fall through the gaps.",
            "intro": "Many of the people we meet have been failed by a system, sometimes over a whole lifetime. Often more than one:",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Child protection and foster care"
              },
              {
                "text": "Family and intimate-partner violence"
              },
              {
                "text": "The legal and criminal justice systems"
              },
              {
                "text": "Substance use and the opioid epidemic"
              },
              {
                "text": "Behavioral health care"
              },
              {
                "text": "Medical care"
              },
              {
                "text": "Financial systems"
              },
              {
                "text": "Climate disaster and food insecurity"
              }
            ],
            "outro": "Services exist, but they are not always within reach of the people who need them most. People tell us they have given up asking for help.",
            "pivot": "Sometimes, we’re able to change that."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec_86eswx3c0q",
      "preset": "starter/stack-12@1",
      "layout": {
